ract simplicial complex K is doubly Cohen-Macaulay over every characteristic-zero field and contains no two-dimensional homology-sphere subcomplex over any field. Homology sphere includes every face link. Thus even a cover by the permitted pieces is impossible, before the overlap or reordering requirements. The finite geometry field F11 is distinct from the CM coefficient field. No subdivision, immersion, enlargement or global-homology-only substitute is used; no CM claim for every prescribed positive characteristic is made.\n\nThe original13-file PR mathematical result is unchanged. The complete new note supplies the faithful GL9 polynomial representation reduction modulo t^9, both neighbor types and normal displacement separation, actual finite abstract quotient and unchanged links, irregular deleted-link normalized gap, weighted cocycle minimizer and factor2, every same-dimension deletion/Reisner case, and characteristic-independent sphere Euler contradiction. No full finite quotient enumeration or entire boundary-matrix computation is claimed. Original inputs/old audit prose are labelled historical; the new paper and verification package are operative.\n\nSubstantial earlier machinery is credited: LSV building/lattice/matrices; Lubotzky-Meshulam degree-versus-congruence separation; Ballmann-Swiatkowski Garland-type vanishing; Januszkiewicz-Swiatkowski curvature obstruction. The particular nonreduced matrix reduction and all deletion conditions are proved here. Root and three full source-first mathematical approaches independently checked the supplied candidate. Root and three extensive priority approaches recorded176 query inputs/167 exact distinct strings, not unique works, and found no earlier recorded full answer in inspected accessible material. This is not a firstness, causal-independence, exhaustive-search or continued-global-openness certificate. Chari1997 and Baclawski1982 full bodies and other original bodies/books/theses/indexes remain material access gaps. Exact versions and selective scopes are retained. [Priority decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/b28ab797744d2fcfd840d78cde3c7d63821fbdd7/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1155_30000214/ROOT_PRIORITY_DECISION.md).\n\nTwo successive NEW no-parent-history whole-package adversarial reviews passed the IDENTICAL six-file release without unresolved issues: [package_01](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/b28ab797744d2fcfd840d78cde3c7d63821fbdd7/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1155_30000214/reviews/package_01/REPORT.md), [package_02](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/b28ab797744d2fcfd840d78cde3c7d63821fbdd7/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1155_30000214/reviews/package_02/REPORT.md). Each sealed its original-target calibration and complete own mathematical analysis before reading prior verdict bodies. These are supplied-candidate internal AI reviews, not blind rediscovery. Earlier body/outline exposure and supplied-source provenance are recorded in the root/family seals.\n\nThe offline runner authenticates all101 frozen authored audit members and final PDF/source identities. Two byte-exact complete745-byte positive outputs, normal and optimized Python, accompany6 actual computed-property wrong-construction failures. All120 source members are authenticated, and extracted normal/optimized rebuilds reproduce allsix files. Tooling40 synthetic fixture groups pass both modes. Optional NumPy local-matrix checks run normally only and refuse -O; historical assert-based programs are distinct. These finite checks support the full symbolic proof and do not establish lattice theory or enumerate K. Third-party source bodies/extracts/renders/raw service returns are excluded; optional full source custody requires independently obtaining private sources.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in developing, writing, researching, computation and adversarial verification. This preprint is **unrefereed**. Internal AI reviews are not external human peer review, journal refereeing or formal proof verification. No human outreach was prepared or initiated.\n\nThe repository production uploader verified the reviewed payloads and supplied metadata, with normalization record []. Google Workspace CLI added exactly one row at `'Math Puzzles'!A169:D169` and verified exact readback. Reviewed source head:`7bc343bc88e5211e06841e375e97015fa8e5d155`. PDF SHA256:`0f3bd7b0b576188794376e5a6428f7049bd19a1e778b68ad5c63b696a73c3a01`. Source/verification ZIP SHA256:`7919adebe0119f34df35e905ebe3665b1d66e79477fa36a06c30801bbe736a5b`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:05:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T01:57:46Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"258f0e71d818312a892bca19ebb451212cc838c5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1155/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1155/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1155/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/7bc343bc88e5211e06841e375e97015fa8e5d155","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:research/30000214-homology-sphere-cover-negative-20261010","ref":"research/30000214-homology-sphere-cover-negative-20261010","sha":"7bc343bc88e5211e06841e375e97015fa8e5d155","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKr